      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Linux Kernel evolves rapidly and, as every software, is&#xA;  subject to bugs.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Some people are trying to find defects in the code by&#xA;  searching for known patterns and known misuse, documented either as part of&#xA;  the kernel API usage or after bugs being known. At Mandriva, and as&#xA;  foundation of my PhD subject, we want to explore another way which is&#xA;  well-known but complex: Model-Checking. Main goal of this talk will be to&#xA;  introduce the subject and present the state of the art around kernel code&#xA;  checking.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
